Takes 4 starting values (for each track) + a list of exercise scores given in this format:

[[Cognition Scores], [Expressive Language Scores], [Receptive Language Scores], [Speech Scores]]

If an area didn't have any scores (the user didn't take any recent tests in that area), the value corresponding to that track 
takes a small decay penalty

The RL model then allocates 10 exercises using the largest-remainder method, to each of the 4 tracks based on what it thinks
the user should spend time practicing. The model favors high scores in weak areas, and penalizes neglecting weak areas
